# Test results
TestResults/
[Cc]overage*.xml
[Cc]overage*.json

# EF Core
*.efmigrationslock.json

# Environment files - real secrets live only in a local, never-committed .env
# (see infra/docker/.env.example, infra/docker/mssql/.env.mssql.example). Matches ".env" and
# any ".env.<suffix>" variant (e.g. web/.env.production, web/.env.development - Vite reads
# these) at any depth, while explicitly un-ignoring ".env.example" / ".env.*.example" style
# templates so they stay trackable. P0-SEC-01 (security-auditor) found the previous bare
# ".env"-only rule missed the ".env.production"/".env.development" shape; this replaces it.
# CI secret-scanning (gitleaks, .gitleaks.toml) is defense-in-depth on top of this.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Editor local-history snapshots (e.g. VS Code "Local History" extension) - can capture
# secrets that were briefly pasted into a file and later removed; never worth tracking.
.history/
